BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws -  Original Acoustic Songwriter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
UID:260930et2l6mPOnEyh1MVqZCZbpw
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique. He draws inspirati
 on from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lou Reed\, Steve Earle\
 , Neil Finn and Ron Sexsmith. All of their music and others have carved a 
 deep groove.\n\nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he developed
  a unique connection to music early on. His father worked as a trash colle
 ctor\, and he would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 recor
 ds. Each find felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records were
  covered in dirt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of dis
 covering new sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop th
 e needle and immerse himself in the music.\n\nHe embarked on a pilgrimage 
 to Texas with just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal wa
 s to dive into the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters. 
 Austin\, known as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countles
 s opportunities for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters' n
 ights became his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, liste
 ning to others share their stories through music.\n\nThese days\, he resid
 es in Sonoma County\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and si
 nger-songwriter for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invites 
 everyone to join him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one perso
 n at a time in this vast and unpredictable world we live in.
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-1003202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
