BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Garden Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T140000
UID:260605gQORQImA5kOEN8VheJcu6w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided tour of the Occidental Arts & Ecology Cen
 ter's demonstration gardens and living landscapes. Led by rotating OAEC st
 aff\, these tours offer an opportunity to explore our diverse food\, medic
 inal\, pollinator\, and native plant gardens while learning about the ecol
 ogical principles that guide our work. \n\nWhen: Tours start at 1 pm ever
 y first and third Saturday of the month\, April through October. \n\nWher
 e: Tours start and end at the OAEC Nursery. 15290 Coleman Valley Rd\, Occi
 dental\, CA 95465. Upper Driveway. \n\nImportant Information:\n\nNo regis
 tration required—just show up!\n\nPlease use the second driveway and par
 k in the upper lot near the greenhouses.\n\nThe tour route includes steep 
 hills and unpaved dirt and gravel paths. Sturdy shoes\, a brimmed hat\, an
 d weather-appropriate layers are recommended.\n\nIf you require mobility s
 upport or have other accessibility needs\, please call ahead so we can acc
 ommodate you. Monday–Friday\, contact the main office at \\(707\\) 874-1
 557 ext. 101.\n\nA highlight of every tour is the OAEC Nursery\, a nonprof
 it nursery dedicated to uplifting ecologically and culturally important pl
 ants. The nursery features a wide selection of perennial food crops\, medi
 cinal and native plants\, and an ever-evolving collection of annual vegeta
 bles and herbs adapted to our region.
LOCATION:Occidental Arts and Ecology Center
URL:https://oaec.org/events/tours/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T120000
UID:260514Bg594FnxW0a5CHLFtcYKcg
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginner
 -friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of P
 etaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Floath
 ouse Petaluma\, you'll take part in this Sonoma County Signature Experienc
 e by spending about 90 minutes on the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, 
 traveling a gentle mile-and-a-half route through “Petaluma’s Longest P
 ark.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft up at docks around town\, fascina
 ting  landmarks\, and riverfront gathering spaces to hear stories about h
 ow this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway” helped shape Petaluma—and 
 how today’s community is continuing to reinvent and reconnect with the r
 iver. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll also learn about the peop
 le\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and river advocates helping shape
  the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything is included in the $75 e
 xperience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local guides\, insider river stori
 es\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses. Finish with plenty of tim
 e for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply hanging out downtown by the w
 ater. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Floathouse Petaluma is a nonpr
 ofit project dedicated to “putting butts in boats and smiles on faces”
  by offering year-round easy access to the Petaluma River in and on people
 -powered water craft through rentals\, events\, classes\, lessons and summ
 er camps.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monica Da Silva
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T000000
UID:260224iNlDxTuS7USFmq5_hpX_YQ
DESCRIPTION:Monica da Silva grew up living between The United States and B
 elém\, Brazil\, a city on the Amazon River. A love of travel and foreign 
 language helped to forge her unique sound. \n\n \n\nParalleling her life\,
  da Silva's music contains an eclectic mix of Brazilian and American influ
 ences. Her sound can be classified as International Fusion\, as it is heav
 ily influenced by Brazilian music\, namely Bossa Nova\, but also incorpora
 tes elements of Lounge\, Electronica\, Indie Pop\, and Worldbeat. Da Silva
  brings her cultural diversity to her songs\, smoothly flowing between Eng
 lish\, Portuguese\, and Spanish.\n\n \n\nIn 2010\, da Silva released her a
 lbum "Brasilissima" . The record featured songs in both of her native lang
 uages - English and Portuguese. The first single "Aí Então"\, “was cho
 sen by Putumayo World Music to be included on their compilation “Brazili
 an Beat”. The upbeat\, psychedelic track "That's Not The Way" was chosen
  by the music director of ESPN to be played during the programming of The 
 FIFA World Cup in 2014\, alongside major recording artists Coldplay\, Sér
 gio Mendes\, Pitbull\, Jennifer Lopez\, The Black Eyed Peas\, Stan Getz\, 
 and Astrud Gilberto. \n\nDa Silva's single "Soldado de Amor" \\(2017\\) ha
 s been featured in the BBC One series "The Replacement”\, in the Paramou
 nt Network series "American Woman"\, and in a 2019 campaign for the design
 er Tory Burch.\n\nHer music has also been featured in the series "Heartlan
 d"\, and in an ad for Patron Tequila. She is currently recording a new\, f
 ull-length solo album\, as well as writing and recording with her project\
 , Complicated Animals.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107954611?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
