BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T170000
UID:260430SruMBs1uCUGXlf1siYi4Og
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gravenstein Mandolin Ensemble
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T210000
UID:2610032fPbRKbCCky4sXbZq1GDUw
DESCRIPTION:Experience the bright\, shimmering sound of strings in harmony
  as the Gravenstein Mandolin Ensemble takes the stage at Occidental Center
  for the Arts. This talented local ensemble brings together mandolins\, ma
 ndolas\, mandocello\, and guitar for a lively musical journey spanning fol
 k traditions\, classical favorites\, contemporary arrangements\, and melod
 ies from around the world. With the mandolin family's distinctive blend of
  warmth\, sparkle\, and rhythmic energy\, the ensemble creates a sound tha
 t is both intimate and wonderfully full. Join us for an afternoon of beaut
 iful music\, community\, and the irresistible charm of many mandolins maki
 ng music together!  Get Tickets The Gravenstein Mandolin Ensemble was form
 ed in 2006 in Sebastopol\, California\, a town famous for its Gravenstein 
 apples. With humble beginnings\, the six original members grew to its pres
 ent size of fifteen\, including the entire mandolin family: mandolins\, ma
 ndolas\, mandocellos\, with additional support from guitar and bass. The r
 epertoire includes music from the Classical Era to the most contemporary w
 orks for modern mandolins\; the geographical range includes music from Ita
 ly\, Spain\, Germany\, Eastern Europe as well as Latin America. Smaller gr
 oups\, or "breakout" ensembles\, often perform a variety of music\, includ
 ing Bluegrass\, Celtic\, Choro\, and more. The GME has performed at the Gr
 een Center at Sonoma State University\, the San Francisco Mandolin Festiva
 l and numerous venues through the North Bay Area. In 2018\, the GME co-hos
 ted the national convention of the Classical Mandolin Association of Ameri
 ca\, held in Santa Rosa. John Metras\, Music Director Gus Garelick\, Conce
 rtmaster First Mandolins: Ed Hance Dana Trillo Second Mandolins: Chris Ecc
 les Bob Baeyen Eddie Guthman Rich Nosker Ella Smith Mandolas: Dan Baron Da
 ve Cohen Jan Kahdeman Mandocellos: Rhonda Berney Jan Hansen Guitar: John M
 etras Bass: Dorian Bartley
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/gravenstein
 -mandolin-ensemble
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
