SUMMARY:Step Into Wonder - The Letting Go Art Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T160000
UID:260930eO8dFOg9a0mBNg9yTV6hXQ
DESCRIPTION:An all-ages community art experience where visitors are invite
 d to paint\, draw\, explore\, and add their marks to collaborative artwork
 s that will continue to evolve throughout the month. Come once or return e
 ach Sunday to see how the galleries change as the community creates togeth
 er.\n\nWonder Sundays are free\, all-ages afternoons inside Step Into Wond
 er: The Letting Go Art Experience—an immersive\, evolving world of glowi
 ng sculpture\, music\, creative play\, and collaborative art.\n\nYou won
 ’t simply look at the art. You’ll become part of it.\n\nExplore the in
 stallations\, respond to creative prompts\, add your own marks to the gall
 ery\, move\, play\, reflect\, and follow your curiosity. Each Sunday\, vis
 itors will contribute something new\, allowing the space to grow and trans
 form throughout the month.\n\nNo artistic experience is needed\, and there
  is no right or wrong way to participate. Come as you are\, stay for as lo
 ng as you like\, and give yourself permission to create freely.
LOCATION:Mare Island Art Studios
URL:https://thelettinggoartexperience.com/all-events/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art FREE October 3-4 Bank of America Museu
 ms on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T170000
UID:2609287QrvwVDuMkOsHC-VGYHWCg
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is October 3-4. \n\nAs a chill settles in the air\, Halloween
  costumes are planned\, and leaves crunch on the ground\, take a moment th
 is busy fall season to enjoy local culture! The Sonoma Valley Museum of Ar
 t has exciting exhibits including brand new installation The Real-Life Art
  History of M. Louise Stanley\, an exhibit sponsored by Bank of America th
 at celebrates a unique Bay Area Figurative artist for her wildly imaginati
 ve narratives and distinctly female perspective\, shaped by her keen obser
 vations of everyday life and setting her apart from her male contemporarie
 s. The exhibit features Sanley’s large-scale acrylic paintings\, gouache
  and watercolor works on paper\, sculptural objects\, sketchbooks\, studie
 s\, photos\, and notes from her personal archives\, showing the artist’s
  perspective across multiple media forms. \n\nBank of America Museums on 
 Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full weekend
  of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Private B
 ank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of America\, M
 errill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for access. 
 \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about.bank
 ofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Clay + Bloom: Ceramics\, Floral Design and Watercolor Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T140000
UID:260920JuwCvQx7_kyuJ63QdnK1eA
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to this multimedia workshop. Two of our seasoned instr
 uctors are teaming up to bring you an extra special collaboration.\n\nIn t
 his event You’ll create a vase for your favorite floral arrangement any 
 time of year\, plus once this piece you’ve created has been fired we’l
 l all reconvene and create both a special floral arrangement specifically 
 for this event and we’ll learn how to paint a watercolor still life comb
 ing all of these elements into a truly unique piece of Art!\n\nThis worksh
 op meets twice\, our first meeting is Sunday October 4th 10am - 2pm where 
 we host you for our clay play and Sunday October 25th 10am - 2pm for our F
 loral arranging and Watercolor Still Life painting \n\nWe’ll cover Cera
 mic Slab Building techniques for our vases\, floral arranging and basic Wa
 tercolor techniques for our still life. \n\nWe supply: \n\nClay\, Slab T
 emplates\, Ceramic Tools\, We’ll provide the Glaze and Glazing once your
  vases have been bisque fired\, all flowers needed for arranging at the 2n
 d meeting of this workshop\, Frog/Floral Structural Mechanics/Floral Tape 
 for arrangements\, watercolors for use day of\, Palettes\, Brushes\, Cups 
 and Paper. \n\nYou will walk away from the workshop with a ceramic vase\,
  a beautiful floral arrangement and a watercolor still life that you yours
 elf have fully created! \n\nLunch provided for a small donation\, \\[plea
 se indicate dietary preferences beforehand if possible\\].
LOCATION:Kickwheel Sonoma
URL:https://kickwheelsonoma.com/products/clay-and-bloom-workshop-with-dean
 na-and-gena-sunday-october-4th
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Oktoberfest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T170000
UID:260914R6heJyR57km7WEkSFrMKAQ
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nEvery Su
 nday from 2:00–5:00 pm\, the Plaza comes alive with an exciting mix of m
 usical styles: blues\, soul\, country\, jazz\, swing\, Americana\, mariach
 i\, and more. With a fresh lineup of acclaimed artists\, there’s somethi
 ng for everyone to enjoy.\n\nSonoma Sundays is all about creating opportun
 ities for the community to come together through the power of live music. 
 Music in Place is excited to bring an incredible range of artists to the P
 laza this summer and continue building connections through music.\n\nSonom
 a Sundays are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the
  Sonoma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the KHR McNeely F
 amily Foundation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and mee
 t us on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-10-4/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
