UID:260504GQc1JkXCfkiuAJMMMnRNCw
DESCRIPTION:A fun community bike ride through the heart of Santa Rosa. Com
 e join us this Tuesday! We roll through the JC and McDonald Ave neighborho
 od\, stop in Courthouse Square\, then on to the taco trucks at Mitote Food
  Park in Roseland for dinner! We depart Mitote at 8:15pm\, ride back throu
 gh Courthouse Square\, then on to Yogurt Farms for dessert. This ride is 8
  miles round trip and rides all year long. Rides canceled for rain and hol
 idays. All riders welcome. Bring the whole family! Meet at SRJC parking lo
 t at 550 Silva Ave. We are renting the use of this parking lot every Tuesd
 ay from 5:30pm to 9:30 pm. Taco Tuesday riders can park in the lot during 
 that time frame for free. Please park cars along the back wall on the east
  side. And stage in the row on the northern side of the lot \\(closest to 
 Silva Ave\\). Meet at 5:30pm\; pedals up at 6pm.
LOCATION:SRJC Parking Lot
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T170000
UID:260930KEarcxvyMU66hw0X5RxhOg
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Independent Projects with Amy Hamley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T210000
UID:260926pMIx8nUTikySutpkcDh_0Q
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday · 6 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nOctober 6 – Novem
 ber 10th\, 2026\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics 
 Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nI
 ntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Fee:\n\n$200\n\nMaterials Fee
 :\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$230\n\nThis is a 6 week session w
 ith instructor\, Amy Hamley. This course is for students interested in exp
 loring both wheel throwing AND handbuilding\, and the combination of both 
 in one class! Learn from Hamley’s years of expertise in the field and en
 joy creating handbuilt\, thrown\, and altered forms. Amy caters each sylla
 bus closely to her group of students\, ensuring that every project fits th
 e desires of participants. This course encourages folks to work on indepen
 dent projects in the class\, receiving one on one support from Amy through
 out the time. This course will include demos\, exercises\, and utilize a v
 ariety of methods to achieve the desired goal for each student. Some proje
 cts may include wheel thrown vases with altered adornments\, best practice
 s for slump and hump molds\, and more.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/independent-projects-august
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
