DESCRIPTION:Election day is right around the corner\, and it's not always 
 easy to get information about who's on the ballot. Learn who is running fo
 r city council and other local offices in your city by watching a candidat
 e forum.\n\nWed\, Oct 7\, 6:00 PM: Santa Rosa City Council\, District 4\n\
 nHear directly from candidates in Sonoma County and ask your own questions
  live on Zoom. Hosted by the League of Women Voters of Sonoma County\, a n
 onpartisan\, nonprofit organization dedication to voter education.\n\nFind
  your city's forum on our event calendar at lwvsonoma.org for Zoom webinar
  links and details. Click the event on the calendar for full details. All 
 forums will be posted to our YouTube channel after each forum.\n\nAll Sono
 ma County forums\n\nMon\, Sept 28\, 6:00 PM: Sonoma City Council\, Distric
 t 1\n\nTue\, Sept 29\, 6:00 PM: Cloverdale City Council\, 3 seats\n\nWed\,
  Sept 30\, 6:00 PM: Windsor Mayor and Town Council\, District 1\n\nThu\, O
 ct 1\, 6:00 PM: Sebastopol City Council\, 3 seats\n\nMon\, Oct 5\, 7:15 PM
 : Healdsburg City Council\, District 2\n\nWed\, Oct 7\, 6:00 PM: Santa Ros
 a City Council\, District 4\n\nThu\, Oct 8\, 6:00 PM: Rohnert Park City Co
 uncil\, Districts 2 and 5\n\nAlso check out these forums from our partners
  this October: • KRCB\, for local broadcasts of Sonoma County Supervisor
  forums • AAUW Petaluma\, for Petaluma Mayor and City Council forums
