BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slow Looking in the Gallery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T140000
UID:26071524mGQnuNUk-FocyiRcsgMg
DESCRIPTION:Slow Looking is an intentional practice of spending a longer p
 eriod of time with a single piece of work. We will have a brief check-in c
 onversation and then engage in at least two slow looking experiences each 
 week. Slow looking goes beyond art appreciation. Research has identified c
 ognitive\, physiological\, and emotional benefits including: Stress Reduct
 ion and Relaxation Enhanced Cognitive Engagement Emotional Depth and Empat
 hy Improved Observational Skills Mindfulness Psychological support Increas
 ed Perceived Beauty Social Connectedness No special knowledge of art or ar
 tists required\, just a sense of curiosity. Some people find it useful to 
 bring a journal or sketchbook as part of their looking tools. Some basic a
 rt materials will be available.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/slow-looking-in-the-gallery-fridays-1
 -2pm/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI Mastery for LEADERS managing AI across the business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T103000
UID:260707g9qunggvHEOh8qeCZud2QA
DESCRIPTION:Using AI to Lead More Effectively Across the Business Artifici
 al intelligence is changing how businesses operate\, but for many leaders 
 the challenge is not hearing about AI. The challenge is knowing what is ac
 tually useful\, where to begin\, and how to lead adoption without confusio
 n or unnecessary risk. The Napa Chamber's AI Mastery for Leaders Workshop 
 Series is designed for owners\, executives\, general managers\, partners\,
  and department leaders who want a practical way to guide AI adoption acro
 ss the business. This is not another generic AI webinar or tool demo. It i
 s an in-person\, small-group workshop series built to help local business 
 leaders understand where AI creates value\, how to introduce it responsibl
 y\, and how to turn it into a practical advantage inside the organization.
  What you will learn and walk away with A practical framework for identify
 ing where AI can create value in your business A governance framework for 
 responsible AI use A clear view of which tasks should stay human-led and w
 hich can be AI-assisted A method for identifying and prioritizing high-imp
 act AI opportunities across departments A better approach to organizing SO
 Ps\, documents\, and internal knowledge for stronger AI output A practical
  process for piloting AI before rolling it out more broadly A draft roadma
 p for your next 6-12 months of AI adoption Who should attend Business owne
 rs Presidents and CEOs General managers Partners Practice administrators S
 enior department leaders
LOCATION:Turner A
URL:https://business.napachamber.com/events/details/ai-mastery-for-leaders
 -managing-ai-across-the-business-10-09-2026-7611
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
