BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dear Evan Hansen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T163000
UID:260911TZdT5uYYpUmoWekO_wrJtw
DESCRIPTION:Poignant\, raw\, and of-the-moment\, Dear Evan Hansen pulls ba
 ck the curtain on the profound desire for human connection in the digital 
 age\, offering an empathetic look at the alienation of young people naviga
 ting modern social pressures.\n\nThe story follows Evan\, a high school se
 nior struggling with severe social anxiety who writes motivational letters
  to himself as a therapeutic exercise. When a troubled classmate dies by s
 uicide with one of Evan’s letters in his pocket\, the boy's grieving par
 ents mistakenly believe Evan was his secret best friend. Desperate to comf
 ort them\, Evan plays along\, spiraling into a web of fabricated emails an
 d internet fame before he must ultimately face the truth.\n\nPowered by a 
 critically acclaimed pop-rock score and the sweeping anthems\, Dear Even H
 ansen is a powerful reminder that we are never truly alone. Spreckels is p
 roud to present the North Bay premiere of this six-time Tony Award winning
  musical!
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Domestic Violence Awarness Month (DVAM) Walk/Stroll & Empowerment 
 Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T140000
UID:260911R9H1S3OhgE6l9RcDslrZug
DESCRIPTION:This DVAM Walk/Stroll & Empowerment Walk brings survivors\, fa
 milies\, community leaders\, and supporters together to raise awareness\, 
 honor lives lost to domestic violence\, uplift survivor voices\, and stand
  united against domestic violence.\n\nYou do not have to be a survivor to 
 participate. Walk for someone you love. Walk in honor of someone we’ve l
 ost. Walk to support survivors. Walk to create change.\n\nThe day will inc
 lude our community Walk/Stroll\, survivor speakers\, local leaders\, music
 \, family-friendly activities\, community resources\, and an Empowerment F
 air.\n\nCome walk with purpose and help us send a powerful message through
 out Vallejo: Survivors are seen. Survivors are supported. Survivors are no
 t alone.\n\nTogether\, We Create Change. With Survivors Always. 💜
LOCATION:Vallejo Marina
URL:https://www.vestsolano.org/events-campaigns
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
