BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Arboriculture 101 for Homeowners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T120000
UID:260905aj20YpBohEu8Y2c97sEokA
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever brought home a tree from a nursery only for it t
 o die a few months or years later? Or purchased a property with mature tre
 es suffering from sparse canopies or leaning oddly?\n\n Join WHG's Livin
 g Collections Coordinator Kat Gritt to learn tips and resources to suppo
 rt your trees' wellbeing\, whether you have a new sapling ready for planti
 ng or mature trees on your property.  \n\nThis class is meant to give 
 participants knowledge and techniques to make the best nursery selections\
 , properly install trees\, and keep them healthy. Kat will cover common l
 andscape tree issues so that participants are better prepared to make dec
 isions about tree placement and horticultural care for a successful home l
 andscape.\n\nCare techniques will be demonstrated on trees in the Western 
 Hills Garden.\n\nInstructor bio: Kat Gritt is the Living Collections Coord
 inator at Western Hills Garden. She has been implementing and educating ab
 out tree healthcare practices at the garden since 2023. Kat is a graduate
  of the Merritt College Landscape Horticulture program with an AS degree i
 n Arboriculture. She is currently in the process of becoming an ISA-certif
 ied arborist and certified aesthetic pruner.
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/arboriculture101-2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
