BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4th Space by Idu House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T230000
UID:260604PwHoexb7ZkSYe0pNkxJKNA
DESCRIPTION:4th Space is a live music and community experience built aroun
 d a simple belief: when artists are given a real stage\, a real room\, and
  a community that actually shows up\, something different happens. Tonight
  is what that looks like.\n\nThe night unfolds in three arcs: Identity\, E
 xpression\, and Release. The experience starts at 6:00 PM before you ever 
 reach your seat. The lobby will be activated with an ambient DJ set\, drin
 ks\, and soft visuals designed to let you settle in and connect before the
  curtain opens.\n\n🎙️ The Lineup\n\nE’mani Aurielle — Live \\(90'
 s/00's R&B & Soul\\)\n\nTyler-Lauren — Live \\(90s R&B\, soul\, and jazz
  fusion\\)\n\nTravie Bobbito — DJ Set \\(Love Supreme SF founder\\)\n\n
 🕒 Run of Show\n\n6:00 PM — Doors & Activated Lobby\n\n7:00 PM — In-
 Theater Opening\n\n7:45 PM — Live Performances Begin\n\nBetween sets\, s
 hort intermissions give you time to breathe\, visit the bar\, and let the 
 night build. Expect live vocals in a room whose acoustics were built for e
 xactly this.\n\nBe in the room. One night only. \\*Tip: Arrive early to ca
 tch the lobby experience before the theater portion begins.
LOCATION:Empress Theatre
URL:https://empresstheatre.org/event/4th-space-by-idu-house/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twist of Fate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T213000
UID:2605293iXpL48_LUWSINBL-dpn2w
DESCRIPTION:Twist of Fate\n\nOctober 10\, 11 & 12\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor\n\nMaxim Lando\, pi
 ano\n\nMATT BROWNE: Divertimento for Orchestra \\(World Premiere\\) FRANZ 
 LISZT: Concerto No. 1 in E-Flat major for Piano and Orchestra\, S.124 PYOT
 R ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Symphony No. 4 in F minor\, Opus 36\n\nThe season’
 s opener begins with a fanfare of fate\, which marks a poignant full circl
 e for Francesco Lecce-Chong. He returns to the first piece he led with the
  Symphony: Tchaikovsky’s tempestuous Symphony No. 4. This high-octane pr
 ogram also features fiery virtuoso Maxim Lando in Liszt’s thrilling Pian
 o Concerto No. 1 and a world premiere by Matt Browne\, a celebrated alumnu
 s of the First Symphony Project.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\, and price
 s are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to availabilit
 y.\n\nPhoto by Chris McGuire
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SUP Yoga on the Petaluma River
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
UID:2603178yqy6iuZfkuQ3jZL_f_JBQ
DESCRIPTION:Slow down and float into a quieter rhythm with SUP Yoga on the
  Petaluma River at The Floathouse Petaluma. Launching from downtown Petalu
 ma\, this peaceful on-the-water yoga experience feels worlds away from the
  bustle—set in the calm\, protected turning basin where the river natura
 lly invites you to relax.\n\nThis all-levels\, 90-minute session welcomes 
 everyone\, from first-time paddle boarders and yoga newcomers to experienc
 ed practitioners. We begin with a short\, gentle paddle from the docks to 
 get comfortable on your board \\(knees are always welcome\\)\, then anchor
  together so tidal movement won’t interrupt your flow. Once settled\, yo
 u’re free to move\, stretch\, rest\, or simply be—guided by expert ins
 truction and supported by the shared energy of the group. Evening sessions
  and morning sessions allow YOU to choose the vibe that suits you best.\n\
 nAll equipment is provided\, including extra-stable paddleboards that are 
 wider and longer than a yoga mat\, designed to help you feel grounded and 
 secure on the water.\n\nPerfect for locals and Bay Area visitors alike\, S
 UP Yoga on the Petaluma River offers a rare chance to experience downtown 
 Petaluma from the water—peaceful\, playful\, and deeply restorative.\n\n
 It’s YOUR river. Come out and play.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/sup-yoga-on-the-petalum
 a-river/18069218/2026-10-10T09
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:2604308mgB3VviykGxpZhcoVJA5w
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
