UID:260921-t9Ni0aeFUO6GCeuMj7o5Q
DESCRIPTION:Open 13 nights only\, join the Doc and his family and step int
 o over 20\,000 square feet of haunted horror in the heart of Santa Rosa. T
 his year we have 2 distinct haunts for you to sink your teeth into.\n\nBli
 nd Scream Haunted House features the all new Caverns of Carnage where wind
 ing tunnels\, claustrophobic chambers\, and forgotten caverns have danger 
 lurking around every corner. The deeper you go\, the harder it becomes to 
 tell what’s part of the cave and what’s watching you from within it.\n
 \nBLACKOUT Haunted House is a pitch-black maze. All you have to guide your
  way is one glow stick… and the creatures stalking your every step. Ever
 y sense will be tested. Every turn is a challenge. And one wrong move… t
 he scream is yours.\n\nFeed your terrors today and get your tickets before
  it's too late. Once the 13 nights are gone\, the haunt disappears until n
 ext year!\n\nLocation - 98 Santa Rosa Plaza\, Downtown Santa Rosa \\(at th
 e corners of 1st Street and A Street\\). South of the Santa Rosa Plaza par
 king garage.
LOCATION:Blind Scream Haunted House
URL:https://www.blindscream.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:260914wfyKB2uKu0ePAcoHBlT8uA
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Drawing Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T140000
UID:260907YcJLX3aiLUuCC0FMAtunBQ
DESCRIPTION:Solano County Arts Council invites you to hang out and draw. T
 his is a weekly\, free event\, open to all!\n\nAfter grabbing some fresh p
 roduce at the Farmer's Market around the corner\, stop by to doodle and dr
 aw in a casual\, fun\, and supportive environment. All ages\, all skill le
 vels. Just a fun place to hang out\, meet new people\, and draw together!\
 n\nBring your own supplies if you can\, limited supplies will be made avai
 lable. Please no inks or paints. Children must be accompanied by parent or
  guardian.\n\nThe art gallery is open during drawing club and showcases lo
 cal original art. The gallery is regularly open Thursdays\, Fridays\, and 
 Saturdays from 10 am to 2 pm\, except second Fridays when it's open from 5
  pm to 9 pm for Vallejo Second Friday Artwalk. We hope you'll stop by!
LOCATION:City Arts Gallery
URL:http://solanocountyartscouncil.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T173000
UID:260831vLjC5gE3LkOMbw11J_AADA
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:260824ers_oUp1eUKdOQcLAROoOw
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Intermediate Hiking for Fitness Fall 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
UID:260823qJOFZQybMUSinlQ0W6G2JA
DESCRIPTION:The program leaders will guide you on 8 weekly hikes
  with the challenge increasing each week. Leaders will have grou
 p discussions about gear\, hydration\, hiking poles\, first aid a
 nd pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for Bald Mountain\,
  where hikers can enjoy stunning vistas.\n\nThe following is a l
 ist of possible routes specifically selected for this hiking seri
 es: \n\n1) Sat 9/26 — Creekside + Waterfall loop\, 3.6 miles\,
  750 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 2) Sat 10/03 – Vist
 a Trail loop\, 3.4 miles\, 830 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Bar
 n\\] 3) Sat 10/10 – Hillside to Neptune table + Meadow\, 4.4 
 miles\, 970 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 4) Sat 10/17 
 – Goodspeed to Nattkemper bench\, 3.8 miles\, 1\,240 ft elevati
 on \\[meet @ Goodspeed lot\\] 5) Sat 10/24 – Hillside + Vista
  Trail loop\, 3.6 miles\, 1\,070 ft elevation \\[meet @ White B
 arn\\] 6) Sat 10/31 – False Lake Meadow & Lake Ilsanjo loop i
 n Trionne-Annadel SP\, 6.1 miles\, 670 ft elevation \\[meet @ An
 nadel's Cobblestone Trailhead\\] 7) Sat 11/07 – Fern Lake + Orc
 hard loop in SDC/Jack London SHP\, 5.5 miles\, 1\,460 ft elevati
 on \\[meet @ Walnut & North St inside SDC\; park on Grove St\\
 ] 8) Sat 11/14 – Bald Mtn summit (w/optional Headwaters detour\
 , 5.8 miles)\, 5.1 miles\, 1\,670 ft elevation \\[meet @ White 
 Barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes are subject to change based o
 n the group and weather\, as the group does hike in light rain
 s. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky or slippery trails\, and 
 layers. Bring water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will 
 be limited to 35 participants. \n\nThe hiking series costs $80 (
 plus a $10 parking fee per visit. Note that the Sugarloaf Annua
 l Pass is $59 and valid at Sugarloaf and Jack London SHP)\, or
  free-of-cost for participants with a September 2026 or newer Pa
 rk Rx from a Sonoma County Medical Provider.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/intfffall26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Andaz Hotel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T000000
UID:2608137-FkrXA3QkKvCKbQT7qVMw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Andaz Napa - A Concept By Hyatt
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108590257?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
