DESCRIPTION:Twist of Fate\n\nOctober 10\, 11 & 12\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor\n\nMaxim Lando\, pi
 ano\n\nMATT BROWNE: Divertimento for Orchestra \\(World Premiere\\) FRANZ 
 LISZT: Concerto No. 1 in E-Flat major for Piano and Orchestra\, S.124 PYOT
 R ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Symphony No. 4 in F minor\, Opus 36\n\nThe season’
 s opener begins with a fanfare of fate\, which marks a poignant full circl
 e for Francesco Lecce-Chong. He returns to the first piece he led with the
  Symphony: Tchaikovsky’s tempestuous Symphony No. 4. This high-octane pr
 ogram also features fiery virtuoso Maxim Lando in Liszt’s thrilling Pian
 o Concerto No. 1 and a world premiere by Matt Browne\, a celebrated alumnu
 s of the First Symphony Project.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\, and price
 s are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to availabilit
 y.\n\nPhoto by Chris McGuire
LOCATION:Green Music Center
