BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Readers' Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T180000
UID:260908CBmnyQOI_06DxGuwTKpOGw
DESCRIPTION:2nd & 4th Tuesdays\, 2-4 pm in the OCA Lobby Interested in lea
 rning\, sharing and reading short plays? Readers Theatre is a fun opportun
 ity to express yourself. Readers Theatre participants read scripts adapted
  from literature\, while the ‘audience' pictures the action by hearing t
 he script being read aloud. It requires no sets\, costumes\, props\, or me
 morized lines. Instead of acting literature as in a play\, the performer's
  goal is to read a script aloud effectively\, enabling the audience to vis
 ualize the action. Performers bring the text alive by using voice\, facial
  expressions\, and some gestures. $15 participation fee\, $10 for OCA memb
 ers. Alternating READER'S CHOICE nights: Can be play\, poetry\, story\, es
 say\, your own writing\, OR ?????? For more information\, email joanjustjo
 an@hotmail.com Joan
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/readers-the
 atre-2-m26cd-ccmap
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
