SUMMARY:An Evening with Gloria Armstrong: Poetry\, Film & Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T193000
UID:260928hxqyP8zEIEujXCtMQK9Sfw
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for an evening with a
 rtist and poet Gloria Armstrong\, featuring poetry\, short films\, and con
 versation in conjunction with her exhibition Spirit of My Homeland: Contem
 porary Indigenous Art by Gloria Armstrong.\n\nGloria will share a selectio
 n of her poetry\, followed by short films about her life\, artistic callin
 g\, and connection to the natural world. Her daughters\, Lorelle Ross and 
 Yana Ross\, will facilitate a Q&A with Gloria about her work and lifelong 
 journey as a contemporary California Indian artist.\n\nThe program will al
 so include short films by Gloria’s granddaughter\, Tavi Carpenter\, and 
 local filmmaker Lee Foster\, with an opportunity for questions following t
 he films.\n\nSpirit of My Homeland is on view September 5–December 18\, 
 2026.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://AnEveningWithGloria.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
