BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Live Music at Spicy Vines feat. Adam Lieb
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T180000
UID:260915iivX1mfK4USSP3H3NKFOAA
DESCRIPTION:Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come t
 ogether.\n\nJoin us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a tast
 ing room experience like no other — where top local musicians from acros
 s the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll an
 d Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new soun
 ds and new reasons to raise a glass. \n\nAdam Lieb\n\nBlending rock\, blu
 es\, soul\, and global folk influences\, singer-songwriter and guitarist 
 Adam Lieb delivers music infused with passion\, craftsmanship\, and deep 
 cultural roots.\n\n Details\n\nNo cover. Walk-ins are welcome\, but this 
 event tends to fill up quickly\, so we recommend making a reservation. We 
 are dog and family friendly!
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/event/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T170000
UID:2609149KMrKa9GAkykpzkRSdvPOg
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Drawing Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
UID:260907pcOdKXeMXESdJ074TfSL7w
DESCRIPTION:Solano County Arts Council invites you to hang out and draw. T
 his is a weekly\, free event\, open to all!\n\nAfter grabbing some fresh p
 roduce at the Farmer's Market around the corner\, stop by to doodle and dr
 aw in a casual\, fun\, and supportive environment. All ages\, all skill le
 vels. Just a fun place to hang out\, meet new people\, and draw together!\
 n\nBring your own supplies if you can\, limited supplies will be made avai
 lable. Please no inks or paints. Children must be accompanied by parent or
  guardian.\n\nThe art gallery is open during drawing club and showcases lo
 cal original art. The gallery is regularly open Thursdays\, Fridays\, and 
 Saturdays from 10 am to 2 pm\, except second Fridays when it's open from 5
  pm to 9 pm for Vallejo Second Friday Artwalk. We hope you'll stop by!
LOCATION:City Arts Gallery
URL:http://solanocountyartscouncil.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T173000
UID:260831kkRZbhh48U-rhG2M2vUrDw
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
