BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch With Sonoma County Author Karen Gebbia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T130000
UID:260924hPF7yNC68UySzpkZ6fukBg
DESCRIPTION:You can't rush real iced tea. Charlotte wants to wait patientl
 y. She really does. But waiting is hard\, especially on a stifling Marylan
 d morning\, when her t-shirt feels like a hot\, heavy blanket\, and she ca
 n't think of anything but Nana's cold\, sweet\, lemony\, real iced tea.\n\
 nThere are so many steps to Nana's secret recipe tea! Steeping\, sugaring\
 , cooling . . . baking muffins to go with it! Nana tells her to find somet
 hing useful to do while she waits\, so Charlotte sweeps\, and swings\, and
  snaps pillowcases\, but it still isn't ready!\n\nCharlotte has to find mo
 re things to do to pass the time\, and soon she finds that a day spent wai
 ting can be a day spent enjoying the slower moments. Sometimes the sweetes
 t things in life are the things we have to wait for\, and learning to savo
 r them slowly is a joy all its own. Included is a reader's note for adults
  on helping kids learn how to wait and a secret recipe to try at home.\n\n
 Scavenger Hunt and Stickers for the kiddos.
LOCATION:Russian River Books & Letters
URL:https://www.booksletters.com/events/book-launch-with-sonoma-county-aut
 hor-karen-gebbia
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pumpkins in the Park: A Santa Rosa Scavenger Hunt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T180000
UID:260923ppgZ58MZx0y1fzjViSg_8A
DESCRIPTION:Think you know our City parks well enough to be able to find t
 he rare pumpkin cutouts?! Here’s how it works… --- DETAILS - Beginning
  Oct. 1\, visit any one of our City parks from the link below and hunt for
  pumpkin cutouts! - Pumpkin cutouts will be eight inches tall and laminate
 d on card stock. - If you find a pumpkin cutout\, the directions on how an
 d where to collect your prize will be on the back \\(also listed below\\).
  The first day you can collect a prize is Oct. 1. - Staff will re-hide the
  pumpkin cutouts for others to find \\(last date of re-hiding is Oct. 23\\
 ). - Oct. 30 will be the last day you can collect a prize for finding a pu
 mpkin cutout. --- MORE INFORMATION Visit SRCity.org/PumpkinHunt for more i
 nformation\, including a list of City parks where pumpkin cutouts will be 
 hidden\, how to collect your prize\, and more.
