DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T130000
UID:260903dAHyDgywU02HXz5s_gkaRA
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free Sponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of sum
 mer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn that 
 was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over just 
 to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, raw m
 ilk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Specialt
 y prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market. Enjoy th
 e intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal place t
 o meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover the a
 bundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Farmers M
 arket\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your dollar i
 nto a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footprint\,
  and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food by mee
 ting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine.  www
 .aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin County Civic Center
URL:https://www.marincounty.org/main/calendar#/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T173000
UID:260831qJDuR9of_Eu5Jqo_Tk5TDQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T170000
UID:260824IZzXygeSAUCpHINf71s4gA
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
