BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blind Scream Haunted House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T220000
UID:260921EkpsgOwL90eT2cVnh29pEw
DESCRIPTION:Open 13 nights only\, join the Doc and his family and step int
 o over 20\,000 square feet of haunted horror in the heart of Santa Rosa. T
 his year we have 2 distinct haunts for you to sink your teeth into.\n\nBli
 nd Scream Haunted House features the all new Caverns of Carnage where wind
 ing tunnels\, claustrophobic chambers\, and forgotten caverns have danger 
 lurking around every corner. The deeper you go\, the harder it becomes to 
 tell what’s part of the cave and what’s watching you from within it.\n
 \nBLACKOUT Haunted House is a pitch-black maze. All you have to guide your
  way is one glow stick… and the creatures stalking your every step. Ever
 y sense will be tested. Every turn is a challenge. And one wrong move… t
 he scream is yours.\n\nFeed your terrors today and get your tickets before
  it's too late. Once the 13 nights are gone\, the haunt disappears until n
 ext year!\n\nLocation - 98 Santa Rosa Plaza\, Downtown Santa Rosa \\(at th
 e corners of 1st Street and A Street\\). South of the Santa Rosa Plaza par
 king garage.
LOCATION:Blind Scream Haunted House
URL:https://www.blindscream.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gain Speaking Confidence with Mare Island Toastmasters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T203000
UID:260916uNZB8AaiqUmNgEiQ6FNC8A
DESCRIPTION:We meet in-person only on the 1st and 2nd Thursdays of the mon
 th. However\, you can catch us online every Thursday unless the meeting da
 te falls on a holiday.\n\nPlease register at https://signup.com/go/WiniixA
 \n\nWhat is Toastmasters About?\n\nUsually at our meetings\, we will have 
 a prepared speech\, and a speech evaluation. The Grammarian and Wizard of 
 Ah's will listen for turns of phrases and the use of filler words. We also
  practice impromptu speaking during the section of the meeting called Tabl
 e Topics. During Table Topics\, at a recent meeting\, we were asked what w
 e felt was the biggest communication problem or challenge. What would you 
 answer in a fast moment? Table topics will challenge you to think quickly 
 and give an answer without preparation.\n\nYou will also hear tips on publ
 ic speaking skills at our upcoming meeting. Whether you're a seasoned trav
 eler or just looking for some adventure from the comfort of your home\, th
 is event is perfect for you.\n\nToastmasters International is all about co
 mmunication excellence\, and for 100 years and counting\, Toastmasters hav
 e been expressing themselves better\, practicing\, and evaluating in a fun
  club environment\, shining all around the world.\n\nTo find out more--Msg
  us on our webpage \\(under Contact Us\\) button at\n\nhttps://mareisland.
 toastmastersclubs.org/\n\nIf you will join us in-person on the first or se
 cond Thursday of the month\, we meet this week at Kaiser Hospital Bldg. A.
  3rd floor meeting room. When you enter the hospital building\, go past th
 e piano to the elevator. Go to the 3rd floor. Exit left out of the elevato
 r and left at the hall. Go past the gym and take a left at the hall. Walk 
 down the long hall to the meeting room.
URL:https://signup.com/go/WiniixA
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T170000
UID:260914SSnhbphnCEC_MTjIbyP6yA
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T160000
UID:260909XGcaoFUGk0Oj35e2UY4_PQ
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T163000
UID:2609093DSCEJ14mEKdXUwG__pWNg
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T120000
UID:2609038SvzFHNYjUaISC-YfOaFng
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique.  He draws inspirat
 ion from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lou Reed\, Steve Earle
 \, Neil Finn and Ron Sexsmith. All of their music and others have carved a
  deep groove. \n\nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he develop
 ed a unique connection to music early on. His father worked as a trash col
 lector\, and he would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 rec
 ords. Each find felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records we
 re covered in dirt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of d
 iscovering new sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop 
 the needle and immerse himself in the music.\n\nHe embarked on a pilgrimag
 e to Texas with just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal 
 was to dive into the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters
 . Austin\, known as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countl
 ess opportunities for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters'
  nights became his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, lis
 tening to others share their stories through music.\n\nThese days\, he res
 ides in Sonoma County\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and 
 singer-songwriter for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invite
 s everyone to join him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one per
 son at a time in this vast and unpredictable world we live in.\n\n“Scott
  Ray Laws is an unique and really cool songwriter…he digs into materials
 \, tells a story in his songs\, and has a clean baritone vocality that is 
 easy on the ears. We had a chance to meet and hang with Scott back in May 
 ..and I HAD to have him back for a Wednesday evening.” Luigi- Owner-The 
 Listening Room.\n\n“..An ORIGINAL songwriter who knows how to tell a sto
 ry clearly in song” -  Scotty O’Neill - Guitarist/Promoter\n\n“ It w
 as such a treat catching your set last night — really refreshing to hear
  something new and original. Thanks for pulling up a chair and hanging out
  with us — we really enjoyed the conversation and the stories behind you
 r songs.”  -Tripp B. - Sonoma Songwriter\n\n“Expect slow burning passi
 on and vivid music …the kind of energy that turns into “let’s stay f
 or just one more!..”  - Doug- Owner/Wine Maker- Spicy Vines\n\n“...His
  lyrics simply tell first-person stories from his own life. Nothing fancy\
 , he's not writing to impress--he pours himself\, as is\, into each phrase
  and melody.”- Rebecca Roudman- Dirty Cello Radio Hour KRCB Radio 104.9 
 FM\n\n“ It is through forthright lyrics that are personal and earnest\, 
 that he composes lyrical pictures. Taking snapshots from the most common w
 alks of life...”  - David Sampson - Producer Studio Secti West\n\n“..r
 elaxed mid-tempo Americana\, capturing in each song the rhythmic pocket La
 ws is known for creating.” -  Coyote Music Review 2024
LOCATION:Café Frida Gallery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108513257?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T170000
UID:260824-oAd_dpo9UijEFBzy1oIUg
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Beat Poetry Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T113000
UID:260820Ufnoqcnq3kmbp1hoVjiyLA
DESCRIPTION:Spoken word artists wishing to share their original poetry on 
 the radio are welcome to join in a live studio broadcast on the 4th Thursd
 ay of the month. Poets take turns at the mic open mic style for an hour lo
 ng poetry show.\n\nThe public can listen to the broadcast on OZCAT 89.5FM 
 KZCT\, or stream online. Hosted by DJ LaLa\, poets have been sharing their
  work live on air since 2018.\n\nPoets should arrive 15 minutes early. The
  venue\, located in a historic Victorian home\, is only accessible via sta
 irs. Please contact Benicia Poet Laureate Emeritus Tom Stanton at skipperw
 icky@gmail.com for the possibility of submitting an .mp3 in lieu of in per
 son performance.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2120553825431551/2120553858764881/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Belly Dancing with Raja - Thursdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T183000
UID:260817UxOHE-kIzEa2Zgv3l7u7_Q
DESCRIPTION:DATE AND TIME: Thursdays\, 5:30 PM\n\nUnlock your inner streng
 th and find your flow. Belly dancing with Raja is an innovative fusion cl
 ass that blends the rhythmic artistry of belly dance with the high-energ
 y benefits of aerobics. Designed to be both a cardiovascular challenge an
 d a deep toning session\, this class focuses on the “powerhouse” of th
 e body—your core.\n\nBy layering fluid\, isolative movements over an ath
 letic aerobic base\, you will challenge your muscles in ways traditional g
 ym workouts can’t reach.\n\nWhat to Expect in Belly Dancing Class\n\n•
  Core-Centric Power: Use undulations and shimmies to engage deep abdomina
 l muscles for a tighter\, stronger midsection.\n\n• Functional Stability
 : Improve your balance and posture through controlled\, hip-driven moveme
 nts and low-impact aerobic footwork.\n\n• Total Body Toning: Build lean
  muscle in your legs\, glutes\, and arms while maintaining a constant\, he
 art-pumping pace.\n\n• Mind-Body Connection: Enhance your coordination 
 and body awareness through rhythmic\, expressive choreography.\n\n“Wheth
 er you’re looking to define your waistline or simply want a workout that
  feels like a celebration\, this class offers the perfect balance of sweat
  and grace.”\n\nDifficulty Level: All levels welcome! No prior dance ex
 perience is required—just bring your energy and a willingness to move.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/belly-dancing-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
