BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rooftop Party at Lovely Hotel for Single Professionals\, 40+
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T210000
UID:261001GvM_l2Fv-0-fv1898aZ9qg
DESCRIPTION:Meet new single friends\, 40+\, at Napa’s most beautiful bou
 tique hotel! Dress to impress.\n\n**TICKETS at www.thepartyhotline.com**: 
 $45**.** The hotel has asked us NOT to collect money at the door\, so you 
 must be on the prepaid list to attend. INCLUDES light appetizers\, served 
 at 3pm\, as long as they last\; plus a FUN Mixer Game\, with prizes. In or
 der to facilitate gender balance\, we are offering you the opportunity to 
 bring a bachelor friend to the party\, free of charge! Please email us at 
 rich@richgosse.com\,after you purchase a ticket\, so we can add his name t
 o the guest list.\n\nWHEN: Sunday\, October 25\, 2026\, 3-5pm.\n\nWHERE: A
 rcher Hotel\, 1230 First Street\, Napa CA 94559. Enjoy both outdoors and i
 ndoors at the lovely Sky & Vine Rooftop Bar. Part of this bar is fully cov
 ered. As you enter the Archer Hotel\, you'll be overwhelmed by the majesti
 c lobby. It will make you feel that you've entered a lobby at one of the
  National Parks. It's that beautiful. Take one of the elevators up to th
 e rooftop outside bar. That's where you'll join us. The surrounding views
  of the downtown area are absolutely amazing. The Archer Hotel is the ta
 llest building in the entire Napa Valley\, with sweeping views from our ro
 oftop party! There are heat lamps and comfortable chairs for us to sit o
 n. Some with a fire pit. Here's your chance to actually meet someone in a 
 casual environment like before online dating was invented. \n\nIf by cha
 nce you stick around until it gets dark\, you can enjoy eating at one of t
 he many outstanding restaurants or walk around the downtown area. Lots o
 f free parking on the street and nearby garages. The Archer Hotel is locat
 ed within easy walking distance of world class restaurants and distinctive
  shops. Our party at The Archer before the pandemic was the subject of a 
 major feature story in *The Napa Register*!\n\nCO-SPONSORED by *The Societ
 y of Single Professionals\, Singles Bay Area*\, and dozens of singles orga
 nizations and meetups. All events benefit The Seva Foundation\, to restore
  sight to the blind.\n\nMORE PARTIES at www.thepartyhotline.com.\n\n·  
       Silicon Valley Speed Dating\, 30s/40s\, Oct 1\, Santa Clara\n\n
 ·        50 & Fabulous\, 50+\, Oct 3\, San Francisco\n\n·    
     Speed Dating for 40s/50s at fun hotel\, Oct 10\, San Francisco\n\n
 ·        Master Speed Dating! Online Seminar\, all ages\, Oct 11\n
 \n·        Salsa Saturday! All ages\, Oct 17\, Novato\n\n·   
      Single and Ready to Mingle\, 50+\, Oct 18\, Tiburon\n\n·    
     Peninsula Speed Dating for 30s/40s\, Oct 25\, South San Francisco\n
 \n·        Rooftop Party at Spectacular Hotel\, 40+\, Oct 25\, Nap
 a\n\n·        Fresh Start Social\, adults of all ages\, Oct  29\,
  San Francisco\n\n·        Halloween Party\, 21-49\, Oct 31\, San 
 Francisco\n\n·        Halloween Party\, 50+\, Oct 31\, Mill Valley
 \n\n·        Halloween Party\, adults of all ages\, Oct 31\, Silic
 on Valley\n\n·        Peninsula 50+ Mixer\, Nov 1\, Burlingame\n\n
 ·        Marin Christmas Mixer\, 40+\, Dec 13\, Tiburon\n\n·  
       Silicon Valley Christmas Mixer\, 50+\, Dec 15\, Campbell
LOCATION:Archer Hotel
URL:https://www.thepartyhotline.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boo! Let’s Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
UID:260930k_DZEJtuA0qOyro4gXeh5Q
DESCRIPTION:Boo! Let’s Dance\n\nOctober 25\, 2026\, at 3:00 pm\n\nWeill 
 Hall\, Green Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong**\, conductor\n\n**Ja
 co Wong**\, SRSYO conductor\n\n**North Coast Ballet California**\n\n**JOHA
 NNES BRAHMS**: Hungarian Dance \\[Ungarische Tänze\\] No. 5 in G minor fo
 r Orchestra\n\n**ARTURO MÁRQUEZ**: Dance \\[Danzón\\] No. 2 for Orchestr
 a (excerpt)\n\n**MAURICE RAVEL**: Suite from *Mother Goose* \\[*Ma mère l
 ’Oye*\\]\n\n**FLORENCE PRICE** (arr. William Grant Still): “Nimble Fee
 t” from *Dances in the Canebrakes*\n\n**JOHANN STRAUSS JR.**: *On the Be
 autiful Blue Danube* \\[*An der schönen blauen Donau*\\] (excerpt)\n\n**A
 LBERTO GINASTERA**: “Danza final” (Malambo) from *Estancia*\, op. 8a\n
 \n**Explore the World Through Music**\n\nDance\, imagine\, and explore wit
 h Snoopy and the Symphony in this lively concert celebrating musical tradi
 tions from around the world.\n\nFrom Brahms’s Hungarian Dance No. 5 to M
 árquez’s Danzón No. 2\, the program travels across cultures through mu
 sic and movement. North Coast Ballet California takes the stage for Ravel
 ’s *Mother Goose*\, while Snoopy adds to the fun in an interactive perfo
 rmance that will have the whole family moving to the music!\n\n*Costumes a
 re encouraged.*\n\n© Peanuts Worldwide LLC\n\n**Programs\, artists\, date
 s\, and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject t
 o availability. All Tickets are nonrefundable.**
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/boo-lets-dance/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee & Collage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
UID:260930j6_shbq8HECmu0i0CS8XDA
DESCRIPTION:Coffee and Collage is Autonomous Gallery’s monthly gathering
  for making art\, sharing space\, and connecting with community.\n\nIn col
 laboration with TBD Coffee\, we invite you to slow down\, grab a cup of co
 ffee\, and spend some time making something with your hands. We provide th
 e collage materials\, tools\, and inspiration. You bring your curiosity.\n
 \nThere’s no experience required and no expectation to make anything “
 good.” Cut\, tear\, layer\, rearrange\, obscure\, discover. Make a mess.
  Follow an idea wherever it takes you. Or just sit at the table and see wh
 at happens.\n\nAt Autonomous\, we believe creative spaces should be access
 ible\, welcoming\, and built around collective care rather than competitio
 n. Coffee and Collage is a chance to practice that together: artists and n
 on-artists\, longtime friends and people meeting for the first time\, all 
 sharing a table and making something side by side.\n\nAll materials provid
 ed. All skill levels welcome.\n\nSuggested donation: $25.\n\nCome Caffeina
 te and create with us!
LOCATION:Autonomous Gallery
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/coffee-collage/20033359
 /2026-10-25T11
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
